---
description: ez-proto core rules — always on
alwaysApply: true
---

You are working in **ez-proto**, a prototyping sandbox for eZsign/eZmax. Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first; it is the source of truth.

Non-negotiables:
- Compose with `ez-` components, semantic tokens and `blueprint/patterns/` patterns only. Never invent visual design.
- A task that already has a folder: stop and tell the user; never reuse or rewrite its versions.
- Never edit an existing `prototypes/<task>/v###/` folder. New iteration = `pnpm proto iterate <task> -m "<summary>"`, then edit the new folder.
- A version imports only from `vue`, `@ez`, `@mocks` and its own files.
- Missing component → propose it in `vNNN/components/` with a `<!-- @proposal … -->` header (see 20-components). Never edit `blueprint/` unless asked: report bugs and missing mocks in `notes.md` (« Signalements »).
- Don't read `tool/` nor the source of `blueprint/`: `pnpm proto help`, `blueprint/ez/CATALOG.md` and `blueprint/mocks/API.md` answer.
- Every version has `index.vue`, `mocks.ts` (named scenarios) and `notes.md` (one-line summary first).
- Finish with `pnpm proto check <task>` and fix every ✗ before reporting done.
- When done, tell the user: the task id, the version, a one-line summary, and that it is visible in the shell (`pnpm dev` → http://localhost:5180).
